\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces t-SNE of the style latent $z_{\mathrm  {s}}$, colored by MNIST digit class, for all six rows of Table\nobreakspace  {}1\hbox {}. Unlike a typical clustering figure, \emph  {color-separated clusters here mean worse} (class information leaking into $z_{\mathrm  {s}}$): separation is visually obvious only for WAE-MMD and F-CS-WAE{} (no per-class MMD)---the two rows with the \emph  {largest} $\Delta _{\mathrm  {inter}}$ in Table\nobreakspace  {}1\hbox {}---and visibly reduced (improved) after adding per-class style MMD. For VAE, $\beta $-TCVAE, and FactorVAE the leakage is statistically real (LP $74$--$87\%$) but not visually apparent in this 2D projection.\relax }}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
